	(title_block
		(title "CostasLink-PYNQ-Z2")
		(date "2026-10-09")
		(rev "A")
		(company "Jason Gallicchio and Claude")
		(comment 1 "Made by gen/schematic.py from gen/pins.py and gen/parts.py")
		(comment 2 "Hardware CERN-OHL-P-2.0, software MIT")
		(comment 3 "https://github.com/QuantumQuasars/OpticsPCBs/CostasLink-PYNQ-Z2")
	)
	(lib_symbols)
	(text "CostasLink-PYNQ-Z2: 5.8 GHz PSK / FSK / QPSK transceiver with a hardware Costas loop, for the PYNQ-Z2 and the Icepi Zero"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 21.59 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 3 3)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "44047133-7264-a7eb-7f68-315aa4fc2325")
	)
	(text_box "Power sheet (left): the header's 28 FPGA signals\nleave as named lines to the receiver, transmitter,\nantenna-switch and slow-path sheets; the window-\ncomparator sheet's nets are joined by the net labels\nat its pins and at the header's.  VR_I and VR_Q are\nthe monitoring DAC's two TX references, from the\nreceiver sheet (where the DAC lives) to the\ntransmitter.  The switch sheet is its own block with\nthree SMAs: fit it to share one antenna (T/R), leave\nit off for two antennas (full duplex on two\nfrequencies)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 190.5 0)
		(size 58.42 26.67)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 194 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "89b74a22-ac26-0aa1-81a4-e2ccf7ec5cd8")
	)
	(text_box "A 5.8 GHz link that carries one or two bits FPGA to FPGA in the speed-of-light time plus about 25 ns of electronics, for quantum\nposition verification; it plugs onto a PYNQ-Z2's or an Icepi Zero's Raspberry Pi header, and two of them talk to each other.  The\nreceiver (sheet 3) is a zero-IF quadrature demodulator whose LO is a synthesizer on a VCXO; a hardware Costas loop steers the\nVCXO, so the LO stays on the far end's carrier and the demodulated I and Q are the constellation point the far end sent, read by\ncomparators straight into the FPGA.  For example, for BPSK, I is the data and Q the phase error; for QPSK and the pilot-plus-\ncorners schemes the four window comparators (sheet 7) decide which way the point left the idle; a slow confirming path (sheet 6)\nvetoes false alarms.  The transmitter (sheet 4) is a quadrature modulator driven by two 2-bit resistor ladders from FPGA pins (and\nTRIG IN, summed into the Q ladder), on its own synthesizer and TCXO.  Sheet 5 is an optional T/R switch for one antenna.  PLAN.md\nhas the arithmetic; sim/budget.py computes it and every blue box quotes it."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 17.78 25.4 0)
		(size 144.78 22.86)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
